/T (Chapter 1 introduces the background, problem, scope and objectives. Chapter 2 reviews the relevant literature on robotic warehousing, single-robot search and multi-agent path finding. Chapter 3 presents the system analysis, requirements and architecture. Chapter 4 describes the environment model, algorithms and their properties. Chapter 5 documents the experimental setup and test cases. Chapter 6 presents results with figures and tables and discusses limitations. Chapter 7 concludes and outlines future work. Appendices list parameters, pseudocode, code excerpts and raw benchmark output.)
