/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 274 0 R
/T (Grid maps. An occupancy grid divides the floor into equal cells, each free or blocked. Grids are simple to generate, fast to search and easy to display, which makes them the standard map for warehouse planning studies [3], [8]. Their drawbacks are coarse geometry and the lack of smooth motion, which are acceptable for a rack-and-aisle layout.)
/E (Grid maps. An occupancy grid divides the floor into equal cells, each free or blocked. Grids are simple to generate, fast to search and easy to display, which makes them the standard map for warehouse planning studies [3], [8]. Their drawbacks are coarse geometry and the lack of smooth motion, which are acceptable for a rack-and-aisle layout.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [49]
>>
