/T (Space-time graphs. A space-time graph adds time as a third coordinate so that a robot may wait. A reservation is a \(cell, time\) pair that other robots may not use [4]. This converts a moving-obstacle problem into a static search problem.)
/E (Space-time graphs. A space-time graph adds time as a third coordinate so that a robot may wait. A reservation is a \(cell, time\) pair that other robots may not use [4]. This converts a moving-obstacle problem into a static search problem.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [51]
>>
