711 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 276 0 R
/T (The proposed system models the warehouse as a weighted grid and provides a library of single-robot planners \(BFS, Dijkstra, A*, Greedy\) behind a common interface. For fleets it adds a prioritised space-time A* planner: robots are planned in priority order, each robot searches over \(x, y, time\) states, and the resulting path is written to a reservation table that later robots must respect. A browser interface served from localhost:8080 shows the warehouse and three robots, and a separate benchmark harness evaluates the planners over randomised scenarios.)
/E (The proposed system models the warehouse as a weighted grid and provides a library of single-robot planners \(BFS, Dijkstra, A*, Greedy\) behind a common interface. For fleets it adds a prioritised space-time A* planner: robots are planned in priority order, each robot searches over \(x, y, time\) states, and the resulting path is written to a reservation table that later robots must respect. A browser interface served from localhost:8080 shows the warehouse and three robots, and a separate benchmark harness evaluates the planners over randomised scenarios.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
