>>
endobj
1050 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 287 0 R
/T (Allowing a robot to wait is essential: without waiting, a robot could not let another pass in a one-cell-wide corridor. A robot that finishes early is not removed from the map. Its goal cell is reserved for every later time step up to the horizon T, and a later robot may enter that cell only before the finishing time. The planner also refuses to accept a goal state at time t if the goal cell is reserved at time t or later, because the robot would have to leave and return.)
/E (Allowing a robot to wait is essential: without waiting, a robot could not let another pass in a one-cell-wide corridor. A robot that finishes early is not removed from the map. Its goal cell is reserved for every later time step up to the horizon T, and a later robot may enter that cell only before the finishing time. The planner also refuses to accept a goal state at time t if the goal cell is reserved at time t or later, because the robot would have to leave and return.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
