1442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 297 0 R
/T (The project shows that a carefully engineered combination of two classical ideas, A* search and space-time reservations, is enough to give small robot fleets optimal routes and conflict-free coordination, and that the claim can be checked with repeatable experiments. The results also highlight where the approach would need to grow: richer motion models, dynamic replanning and larger fleets.)
/E (The project shows that a carefully engineered combination of two classical ideas, A* search and space-time reservations, is enough to give small robot fleets optimal routes and conflict-free coordination, and that the claim can be checked with repeatable experiments. The results also highlight where the approach would need to grow: richer motion models, dynamic replanning and larger fleets.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
1443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 297 0 R
/T (Shorter, conflict-free routes reduce robot travel time and the energy used per task, and fewer collisions and stoppages reduce damage and downtime. Transparent, open planners lower the barrier for small warehouses and training institutes that cannot afford commercial fleet software. Because routes are explainable and measurable, supervisors can audit the behaviour of the fleet. Automation of internal transport also changes the nature of warehouse work, so adoption should be accompanied by training for staff in supervision and maintenance roles.)
/E (Shorter, conflict-free routes reduce robot travel time and the energy used per task, and fewer collisions and stoppages reduce damage and downtime. Transparent, open planners lower the barrier for small warehouses and training institutes that cannot afford commercial fleet software. Because routes are explainable and measurable, supervisors can audit the behaviour of the fleet. Automation of internal transport also changes the nature of warehouse work, so adoption should be accompanied by training for staff in supervision and maintenance roles.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
