4098 0 obj
<<
/Title (Warehouses and fulfilment centres increasingly rely on fleets of autonomous mobile robots to move goods between storage racks and packing docks. The efficiency of such a fleet depends on two coupled problems: finding a short, safe route for each robot through a cluttered, aisle-based floor plan, and ensuring that several robots sharing the same aisles never collide or deadlock. Naive solutions plan each robot independently with a shortest-path algorithm; this produces cost-optimal individual routes but, as this project shows, frequently yields robots that occupy the same cell or swap positions in the same time step.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3910 0 R
/Next 4114 0 R
>>
endobj
