4636 0 obj
<<
/Title (The motivation of this project is to build an academically rigorous and reproducible prototype showing how classical artificial intelligence search techniques, combined with a simple reservation mechanism, can deliver optimal single-robot routes and conflict-free multi-robot plans in an aisle-based warehouse.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4605 0 R
/Next 4637 0 R
>>
endobj
4637 0 obj
<<
/Title (The scope covers: \(i\) a weighted grid model of a rack-based warehouse; \(ii\) implementation of BFS, Dijkstra, A* and Greedy Best-First planners in Java 21; \(iii\) a prioritised space-time A* planner for fleets of robots; \(iv\) a browser-based interface served on localhost:8080 that displays the warehouse and three robots; and \(v\) a benchmark harness that measures path cost, nodes expanded, optimality rate and conflict counts over randomised scenarios. The warehouse layout, robot kinematics and task arrivals are simulated; no physical robots or live sensor data are used.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4605 0 R
/Prev 4636 0 R
>>
endobj
