/Title (query that ended inside the dock, A* expanded 736 nodes against 741 for Dijkstra, almost no saving. The Manhattan heuristic assumes cost 1 per move, so it underestimates the true cost of the dock cells and cannot guide the search well. A heuristic that includes the dock cost, such as a precomputed lower bound, would help. This is why a more typical query was chosen for Figure 6.4, while Table 6.1 reports the average over random queries.)
