/Title (In a basic robotic warehouse, each robot is given a destination and computes or follows a route without considering the plans of the other robots. Typical limitations are: routes that minimise hop count rather than traversal cost; repeated full-floor searches; and collisions or stand-offs in narrow aisles that must be resolved by stopping robots or by operator intervention.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4936 0 R
>>
