<<
/Title (BFS: a FIFO queue that minimises the number of moves and ignores cell costs; the cost of its path is computed afterwards for comparison.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5141 0 R
/Prev 5173 0 R
/Next 5149 0 R
>>
endobj
5161 0 obj
<<
/Title (Let C* be the optimal cost from start to goal. Because h is admissible, every node n on an optimal path satisfies f\(n\) = g*\(n\) + h\(n\) <= C*. A* always expands a node with the lowest f value, so when the goal is first removed from the open list its f value equals its g value and no unexpanded node has a lower f; no cheaper path can therefore exist. With a consistent heuristic, f values are non-decreasing along any path and each node is expanded at most once, which is the property exploited by the closed list. This explains why A* returned the same cost as Dijkstra on every benchmark query.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5150 0 R
>>
endobj
